    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe codebase already had a read-only computed field, `displayName`, wired through the same generated-DTO + MapStruct path. I mirrored that exact pattern for `initials` rather than inventing a new mechanism:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(initials(owner))\")` and a small `initials(Owner)` default method:\n   ```java\n   default String initials(Owner owner) {\n       return owner == null ? null\n           : Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n           + Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \".\";\n   }\n   ```\n\nThis keeps the derivation logic as a single-responsibility unit next to its sibling `displayName`, so `RespondWithOwner` and every other endpoint that maps an `Owner` gets `initials` for free \u2014 no duplication in the function pipeline classes.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComputesInitials` (john/smith \u2192 `J.S.`) passes, and `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures across the suite.",
